the appalachian region of eastern  kentucky is under water several days of  rainfall have caused rivers to overflow  their banks and entire towns to barely  remain above water lines  the area got two months worth of  rainfall in the matter of just two days  with recovery and rescue efforts ongoing  in some areas the flood waters have not  even crested yet  for those residents who did survive the  storm they told stories of horror  everything's going like  everything is gone  the whole life is gone  i was like i don't want this apartment  to buckle with me in it so  i just kind of was like i'd rather be in  the woods than  be inside the apartment  the flash flooding is so severe even  rescuers were shocked by what they were  dealing with probably 95 of the people  in this area here's lost everything  houses cars  animals  it's  it's heartbreaking it really is  these four siblings were all swept away  in the floodwaters  they drowned and their bodies have all  been recovered  the governor who declared a state of  emergency on friday toured the  hardest-hit areas  elsewhere in america overnight monsoon  rains in las vegas flood waters seen  coming through the roof of at least one  of the city's famous casinos  there was also flooding in west virginia  and hundreds were rescued from flood  waters in missouri  while parts of america are soaking wet  other parts are melting  it all comes after the northeast of the  u.s saw unseasonably and dangerous  record high heat earlier this month and  meteorologists know what's causing it  these type of events that have been  occurring over the last couple of weeks  across the country are directly  attributable to climate change  these are big signals extreme heat heavy  downpours  that harken back to the changes in our  atmosphere because of the additional  carbon because of the warming  in kentucky cleanup will mostly have to  wait because they're still in the search  and rescue phase of this storm  officials say the death toll is likely  to climb  gabriel lozando al jazeera
 

